# Application options for the AQT7 firmware. Set them in prj.conf.

mainmenu "T26 AQT7"

config AQT7_DEBUG_PRINT_MS
	int "Period of the sensor values log (ms), 0 = off"
	default 100
	help
	  The debug thread logs the brake pressures, suspensions and NTC with
	  their ADC values on the console every this many milliseconds, like
	  execute_100ms_tasks() in the STM32CubeIDE firmware. 0 turns it off;
	  the acq7 debug snapshot is updated either way.

config AQT7_SIM
	bool "\"sim\" shell command to simulate the ADC sensor inputs"
	default y
	depends on SHELL
	help
	  Adds "sim set/mv/off/show" to the shell: any ADC channel (brake,
	  susp_l, susp_r, ntc) can be replaced by a value typed on the console.
	  The value goes through the same filter and conversions as a real
	  sample, so the brake light and the CAN frames follow it.
	  Turn it off for the car so a stray console byte can't fake a sensor.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
